WEBVTT

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.990
"I'm sorry... I messed up..."

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.980
I'm sorry... I messed up...

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.990
<b>Episode 22</b>

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.990
<b>Dr. Yosano's Whoopsies!
 Forgetfulness</b>

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:21.990
It's gone!

00:00:21.990 --> 00:00:23.980
Where could it be?!

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.460
I'm missing one of the 
scalpels I need for surgery.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:26.630
<b>Scalpel</b>

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:27.970
<i>It's not in my drawer.</i>

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:29.490
<i>It's not under the beds.</i>

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:34.140
<i>I even checked in my pen holder 
and my chopstick case. I still can't find it.</i>

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:34.880
<i>No...</i>

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.630
<i>I haven't forgotten it inside one 
of my recent patients, have I?</i>

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:38.640
<b>Famously attractive
 Doctor Y</b>

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:38.640
<b>Medical 
malpractice?!</b>

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:39.390
<b>Scalpel left 
inside body
causes severe
 injury!!</b>

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:50.400
<b>Management comes under scrutiny!!!</b>

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:46.980
<i>The last three people I operated on 
were Atsushi, Tanizaki, and Kunikida.</i>

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:50.400
<i>If I've forgotten my scalpel 
inside any of them...</i>

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:52.490
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:54.090
<i>I need to check on them, quickly!</i>

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:55.300
Hey, Yosano-sensei.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.970
Thank you for your help the other day.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:00.160
I'm full of life now.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.780
<i>I know.</i>

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.200
<i>Let's play it cool and ask him casually.</i>

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.790
<i>"Atsushi, have you noticed 
anything odd lately?"</i>

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:07.140
<i>Yeah, that's good.</i>

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:11.600
Atsushi, have you tried 
not being odd lately?

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.300
That was unexpectedly mean!

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:16.460
I'm sorry for the way I live my life.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.440
No, that's not what I meant...

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:20.130
<i>Shoot!</i>

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:21.910
<i>I got nervous and messed up.</i>

00:01:21.910 --> 00:01:23.430
<i>Let's try again.</i>

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:26.820
S-Say, the weather's nice today, huh?

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.060
It'd be a nice day to open 
a window to your guts.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:30.660
Do you have trouble speaking?

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:32.930
What exactly do you have in mind?

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:35.560
You aren't going to turn me 
into a tiger rug, are you?

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.080
N-No, Atsushi!

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:40.770
My stomach hurts all of a sudden.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:41.820
Ow, ow...

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:44.050
<i>It's exactly as I feared!</i>

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.330
<b>Famously attractive
 Doctor Y</b>

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.330
<b>Medical 
malpractice?!</b>

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:45.330
<b>Scalpel left 
inside body
 causes severe
 injury!!</b>

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:45.330
<b>Management comes under scrutiny!!</b>

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:46.830
<b>Milk</b>

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:46.830
<b>Moo~</b>

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:51.290
The milk in our apartment 
expired two weeks ago.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:53.220
I didn't want it to go to waste.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:56.530
Don't I always tell you 
to mind the expiry date?

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.330
Sorry, Kyouka-chan, I can't 
deal with this right now.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.720
<b>× Medical Malpractice</b>

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.720
<b>✓ Food Poisoning</b>

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:03.200
<i>Whew!</i>

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:05.080
<i>Let's ask Tanizaki next.</i>

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:07.790
Yosano-sensei.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:09.240
Can I help you?

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:22.740
<b>Operating Room</b>

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:10.950
<i>Stay calm.</i>

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.250
<i>Just be up front.</i>

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:15.350
<i>"I may have forgotten a 
scalpel inside your body."</i>

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:16.520
<i>Let's go with that.</i>

00:02:16.520 --> 00:02:19.270
Tanizaki, let me get straight to the point.

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.730
I can't forget about your body.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:26.610
<i>I got nervous again!</i>

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:29.260
No, I meant to say...

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:30.120
<i>I won't make another medical 
error like this again.</i>

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:33.020
It was a mistake I'll never make again!

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:37.370
I-It's not what you think, Naomi!

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:39.280
You need to show me your body.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:40.720
It's for the best, for both of us.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.490
Wait, Yosano-sensei!

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:43.880
Naomi!

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:45.270
This is a misunderstanding!

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:46.830
Now, come to the bed!

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:49.520
What have I done to deserve this?!

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:54.650
<b>Surgery In Progress</b>

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.480
Why?

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:59.370
<i>Tanizaki's clear, too!</i>

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:00.780
<i>Now...</i>

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:02.970
Kunikida!

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:04.460
How you feeling?

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:06.720
All better now, thanks to you.

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.140
A tired mind is a tired body.

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:10.840
You should be careful.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.170
Thank you.

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:16.790
When you're tired, do you ever have the 
sensation of a blade touching your organs,

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:19.520
or feel as though there's a 
metal object still inside?

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:22.160
What kind of exhaustion could cause that?

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:26.100
<b>Ideals</b>

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:26.100
<b>Scratch 
scratch</b>

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.200
What is the disease called?

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.110
I'd like to know for reference.

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:27.320
S...

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:28.160
S?

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.130
Stress!

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:31.490
Stress is horrible!

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:32.740
It is.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:34.480
Stress can put a hole in your stomach.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.950
It might even form a metal object 
in the shape of a scalpel.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:40.790
A metal object in the shape of a scalpel?!

00:03:40.790 --> 00:03:42.510
It can be that specific?

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:44.280
It's fine as long as you're careful,

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:47.620
but let me know if you notice anything 
and I'll open you right up.

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:49.820
I'll get it done in three minutes.

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:51.880
Like cup noodles?!

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:55.520
<i>It's not in Kunikida, either.</i>

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.760
<i>Maybe I should check, 
like I did with Tanizaki.</i>

00:03:58.760 --> 00:03:59.980
Oh, there she is.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.870
<i>Or maybe I should...</i>

00:03:59.980 --> 00:04:01.340
Yosano-sensei.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.300
We found your scalpel.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:03.940
Eh?

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:05.770
Where did you find it?

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:11.280
Remember when we had a grilled fish party 
with Dazai-san's briquettes and coal stove?

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:11.270
<b>My briquettes!</b>

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:14.790
You were drunk, and you tried 
to gut the fish with a scalpel.

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:18.580
We found it with the cooking utensils.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:20.890
<i>Thank goodness!</i>

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:25.010
All she did was take my X-rays!

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:29.540
<b>Episode 23</b>

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:29.540
<b>Miscellany on 
Shrimp Tails</b>

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:33.650
Lunch today is a bit of a splurge!

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:36.480
Shrimp bowl delivery!

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:38.240
Time to eat!

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:44.770
Lastly, the shrimp tail...

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:46.310
Atsushi-kun! Just a second!

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:50.820
You aren't going to eat the 
shrimp handle, are you?

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:54.410
Dazai-san, what exactly do 
you mean by shrimp "handle"?

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:55.930
Oh, you didn't know?

00:04:55.930 --> 00:04:57.820
The shrimp handle is here.

00:04:58.260 --> 00:04:59.790
The chicken's handle is here,

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:00.890
and the banana's handle is here.

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:04.520
It's not like food was <i>made </i>
that way for our convenience.

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:06.700
Well, you can call it whatever you like.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.470
What are you going to do 
with the shrimp handle?

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:11.970
You seem to care a lot about what it's called.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:13.570
I'm going to eat the tail.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:17.090
That's such a wasteful thing to do 
that you're no longer a valid human!

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:17.080
<b>No longer a
 valid human</b>

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:22.720
Your wasteful treatment of the shrimp tail 
has awakened a new ability in me.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:24.140
Wasteful?

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:25.510
I'm not wasting it!

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:26.910
I'm eating it!

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:29.570
What am I supposed to 
do with the tail, then?

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:31.480
What you do, Atsushi-kun...

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:34.090
is you bury it in the dirt,

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:37.180
so you can harvest it again.

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:38.900
That's disgusting.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.100
And ridiculous!

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:44.730
Pea sprouts grow back with some 
water even if you cut them.

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:48.120
So do branches that you bury in the ground.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:49.550
And so do shrimp.

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:51.780
I fear your concept of shrimp.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:53.470
I'm going to eat it.

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:56.420
W-W-Wait, Atsushi-kun!

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:59.370
You know a watermelon is a vegetable 
and not fruit, too, right?

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.540
Shrimp might be a kind of plant, as well!

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:04.400
You're pushing it now.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:05.950
Aw...

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:07.870
Akutagawa-kun believed me.

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:11.640
<b>Stare...</b>

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:11.640
It's still not sprouting.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:13.500
<i>Poor Akutagawa!</i>

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:15.500
Did you actually tell him that?

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:16.470
I didn't.

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:17.400
Which is it?!

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.810
Hey, whatcha doing?

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:22.410
I'm going to dob you guys in 
if you aren't working.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:24.690
No, you've got the wrong idea, Rampo-san.

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:29.710
We were talking about how you can bury 
a shrimp tail in dirt to get it to sprout.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:32.030
<b>Ahaha!
 That's hilarious!</b>

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:32.030
<i>Ahaha! That's hilarious!</i>

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:33.780
Seriously?

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:35.290
That's obviously not true.

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:36.340
Yes, sir.

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:38.530
<i>Of course.</i>

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:44.910
<i>Man, that kind of ruined my lunch.</i>

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:48.800
Although, if there were such thing 
as an infinitely regrowing shrimp...

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:52.170
<i>Dazai-san seems especially persistent today.</i>

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:57.040
It might be an instant 
solution to world hunger.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:58.770
<b>Gurrrgle</b>

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:02.910
It might solve my hunger, too.

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:05.310
<i>Is he trying to say...</i>

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:08.710
I guess there was no shrimp bowl for me.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:11.330
<i>Has he been bugging me this 
whole time because...</i>

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:14.440
I wish I could have had at 
least the tail of the shrimp.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:18.180
<b>Moral of 
the story:</b>

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:18.180
<b>Ask others 
when 
ordering 
food</b>

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:21.260
They still aren't growing.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:22.710
<i>Akutagawa-senpai...</i>

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:24.720
<i>I'll have some tempura batter ready for you.</i>

00:07:29.630 --> 00:07:31.600
This is hard.

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:35.600
<b>Episode 24</b>

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:35.600
<b>Me Drawing You
 Drawing Me</b>

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:37.480
I-I'm done.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:39.510
Dazai-san.

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:40.970
It sucks, though.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.140
Wow, that looks just like me.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:43.990
That's great.

00:07:43.990 --> 00:07:45.520
Really?

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:48.380
How's yours coming, Dazai-san?

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:50.780
I'm having a hard time.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:52.480
I think I might give up.

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:53.510
Oh, come on.

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:54.750
Let me see.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:56.360
Aw, fine.

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:57.760
<i>I wonder if there are things even 
Dazai-san has trouble with.</i>

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:58.110
Here, take a look.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.280
I'm having a hard time drawing 
the person behind you.

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:03.590
Behind me?!

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:05.480
I don't see anyone!

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:06.350
Dazai-san!

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:08.190
I-I'm done, too.

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:09.190
Cool.

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:10.920
Akutagawa!

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.520
Stop coming in through the window!

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:14.460
It's not a big problem.

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:15.470
It's a huge problem!

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:18.800
Dazai-san, please take a 
look at my drawing, too.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:20.540
Eh, no thanks.

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:21.610
So blunt.

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:24.600
<b>My 
master</b>

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:28.650
<i>Wow, he's really expressing himself.</i>

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:29.930
Atsushi-kun, deal with it.

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:30.990
What?! Come on!

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:32.450
You know...

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.290
You could read the room a little.

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:37.770
You intend to lecture me, you animal?

00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:39.030
Hear me out.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:41.230
You could draw me, too, for example.

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:43.020
Oh, is that what you want?

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:45.020
I've already done that.

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:47.670
You were practice,
before I drew Dazai-san.

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:50.120
Yay. That doesn't make me happy at all.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:51.010
Let's see.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.840
<b>The Weretiger
 I Cut</b>

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:52.830
I'm cut in half!

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:54.880
Why'd you have to choose this scene?!

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:56.210
What else would there be?

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:58.710
That wasn't even me!

00:08:58.710 --> 00:09:01.020
It was an illusion Tanizaki-san made!

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.470
Why don't we make it real, then?

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.110
Ooh, a fight.

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:06.740
This is getting fun.

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:07.780
Oi, Senpai!

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:09.670
Quit enjoying this... Sir!

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:13.200
How dare you speak to Dazai-san 
like that, weretiger?!

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:15.350
Now I'm pissed!

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:17.880
Stop barking! I'll split you in two!

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:18.890
I won't let you!

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:22.140
Yeah! Get each other!

00:09:18.890 --> 00:09:20.260
Yes, you will!

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:28.940
<i>I drew them, too, but I don't think 
I'll be able to show them for a while.</i>

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:35.030
Hey, yo!

00:09:38.690 --> 00:09:42.230
All right, everyone! 
Let's draw Dazai-san together!

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:47.000
A bento box with two pickled plums

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.140
Yes! I'm getting kamaboko today!

00:09:49.140 --> 00:09:53.020
You take a bite, and it starts raining

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:57.240
But don't forget to smile!

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:03.190
Wrap him in bandages
and you get Dazai-san

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:32.990
Violence now would be senseless.

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:34.680
How about a different challenge?

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:36.280
Tell me what you want.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.190
A kitty pet-off!

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:39.440
What?!

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:41.450
<b>Meow</b>

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:42.830
Very well.

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:43.610
Yes.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:44.800
Really?
